data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1480,"item_id":"fc_0160c626cb793549016adb685fabe8819188dba0145c499b05","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"checks\":{\"source_route_and_coverage\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"R001 has direct inputs H001–H004 and output P, implemented in source paragraphs S001–S008. The proposed plan has only one step, T001 : True, with every source paragraph attached to it. Its type proves none of the basis/action formulas, matrix-unit identities, coordinate-module and rank-one facts for the arbitrary localized lattice, scalar-extension/action correspondence, invariant-subspace argument, or final irreducibility. The explanations in the prior proposal do not supply missing typed results. Thus neither paragraph coverage nor the source inference/output boundary is implemented.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/direct_boundaries/R001\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"}]},\"parameters_and_allowed_inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The source parameters and H001–H004 are the only direct inputs to R001. The contract instead binds K, p, lam, M with generic group/module instances, and repeats H001–H003, but declares H004 : True and conclusion : True. No actual type encodes the complex highest-weight module, highest-weight vector and relations, its dimension, an arbitrary admissible lattice, or the divided-power preservation condition. The generic M interface therefore does not establish the source's arbitrary-lattice premise; treating H004 as True also makes the hypotheses unavailable rather than faithfully representing them. The source includes all prime p, lambda=0 and p=2; these cannot rescue absent model data.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/0\"},{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/1\"},{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/2\"},{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/3\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/inputs\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/parameters\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises/3/type\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/6\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]},\"representations_and_conversion_obligations\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The source identifies the target as M tensor_Z K and its construction through the localized lattice, reduction modulo p, and scalar extension; S004 requires basis and x,y,h action correspondence. The contract has no representation definitions or shared obligations (representation is merely \\\"test\\\", objects are empty); the sole plan type True provides no module carrier, action operators, bases, or conversion maps. Consequently there is no demonstrated representation of the arbitrary lattice or typed conversion between M tensor_Z K and any Lean realization, nor any proof of basis/action compatibility or endpoint behavior. This is a missing interface, not a difficult unproved bridge.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"source-context.md\",\"pointer\":\"/42\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument/4\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/objects\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/shared_obligations\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"}]},\"statements_and_local_plans\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The complete elaborated type in type-Check.lean has parameters K with Field K, p with CharP K p and Nat.Prime p, lam with 0≤lam<p, and a generic additive group/module M; H001–H003 are repeated and H004 is True. Its result is True. This is not the source theorem or any nontrivial local obligation. Contract premises H004 and conclusion are both True, and plan T001 is True despite being mapped to all eight source steps. No conditional statements representing the source inferences exist for assembly to discharge; successful elaboration only verifies this vacuous type.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/3\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/6\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/terminal\"}]}},\"findings\":[{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"H004 has been replaced by True. The actual Lean binders contain no V, complex Lie operators, highest-weight vector, dimension assertion, lattice basis/embedding, or divided-power admissibility. Accordingly the proposal does not encode the source assumptions about an arbitrary admissible lattice.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses/3\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises/3/type\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/6\"}]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"Source conclusion P asserts irreducibility of M tensor_Z K. The actual contract conclusion and elaborated Lean result are True, and there is no source-facing theorem type or output map proving P.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/source_outputs/P\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/6\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"T001 is True while purporting to cover S001–S008. It exports none of the source's intermediate mathematical conclusions, so the plan is not a typed implementation of the accepted argument route and has no meaningful internal hypotheses to discharge.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/source_steps\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/terminal\"}]},{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"No typed representation or conversion obligations realize the source's M tensor_Z K construction or S004 basis/action correspondence. Empty objects/shared obligations and the placeholder representation label cannot establish these identifications.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/objects\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/shared_obligations\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"}]}]}}"}

